"{\n  \"entities\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"English\",\n      \"type\": \"Language\",\n      \"description\": \"English is a West Germanic language that originated from the Anglo-Frisian dialects brought to Britain in the 5th to 7th centuries AD by Anglo-Saxon settlers. It has evolved through various stages, including Old English, Middle English, Early Modern English, and Modern English, and is now one of the most widely spoken languages in the world.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Origin\": \"5th century AD, brought by Anglo-Saxons\",\n        \"Periods\": \"Old English (5th to 11th century), Middle English (11th to 15th century), Early Modern English (late 15th to mid-17th century), Modern English (mid-17th century to present)\",\n        \"Influences\": \"Germanic languages, Old Norman (a dialect of Old French), Latin, and others\",\n        \"Number of Speakers\": \"Over 1.5 billion people worldwide\",\n        \"Status\": \"Global language, lingua franca of international communication, business, and diplomacy\",\n        \"Characteristics\": \"Highly inflected in Old English, underwent significant transformations including the Great Vowel Shift, and continues to evolve with the influence of technology and globalization\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"English language\",\n      \"type\": \"Language\",\n      \"description\": \"The English language is a West Germanic language that has evolved over the centuries through various influences and transformations, from Old English to its current status as a global language. It is known for its resilience, adaptability, and rich vocabulary, reflecting the diverse cultures and peoples that have contributed to its development.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Origin\": \"5th century, brought by the Anglo-Saxons\",\n        \"Periods\": \"Old English (5th to 11th century), Middle English (11th to 15th century), Early Modern English (15th to 17th century), Modern English (17th century to present)\",\n        \"Characteristics\": \"Resilience, adaptability, rich vocabulary\",\n        \"Status\": \"Global language\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"5th century\",\n      \"type\": \"Time Period\",\n      \"description\": \"The 5th century marks the period from the year 401 to 500 in the Julian calendar. It is a significant era in the history of the English language and the settlement of the Anglo-Saxons in Britain.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Start Year\": \"401\",\n        \"End Year\": \"500\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Geoffrey Chaucer\",\n      \"type\": \"Person\",\n      \"description\": \"Geoffrey Chaucer is a renowned English poet and author, best known for his work \\\"The Canterbury Tales,\\\" which is a prime example of Middle English literature.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Occupation\": \"Poet and Author\",\n        \"Era\": \"Middle English Period\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"William Shakespeare\",\n      \"type\": \"Person\",\n      \"description\": \"William Shakespeare is considered one of the greatest writers in the English language, whose works exemplify Early Modern English.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Occupation\": \"Writer, Playwright, Poet\",\n        \"Language\": \"Early Modern English\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Australian English\",\n      \"type\": \"Dialect\",\n      \"description\": \"Australian English is a major variety of the English language, developed and spoken in Australia.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Origin\": \"Developed in Australia\",\n        \"Time Period\": \"Modern English period (after mid-17th century)\",\n        \"Status\": \"Widely spoken dialect\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"entertainment\",\n      \"type\": \"Domain\",\n      \"description\": \"Entertainment is a domain that significantly contributes to the global importance and spread of the English language, encompassing various forms of media and cultural activities.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Contribution to English\": \"Significant role in spreading and cementing the importance of English globally\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Old English\",\n      \"type\": \"Language\",\n      \"description\": \"Old English, also known as Anglo-Saxon, was spoken in England from the 5th to the 11th century. It was a highly inflected language with a complex grammar system and a vocabulary heavily influenced by Germanic languages.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Old Norman\",\n      \"type\": \"Language\",\n      \"description\": \"Old Norman was a dialect of Old French spoken by the Normans, who became the ruling class in England after the Norman Conquest in the late 11th century.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"William Caxton\",\n      \"type\": \"Person\",\n      \"description\": \"William Caxton was an English printer and publisher who introduced the printing press to England in the late 15th century.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"British Empire\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Entity\",\n      \"description\": \"The British Empire was the largest empire in history and a major global power from the 18th to the 20th century.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Technology\",\n      \"type\": \"Field\",\n      \"description\": \"Technology encompasses the tools, methods, and processes used to create, develop, and improve products and systems.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Science\",\n      \"type\": \"Field\",\n      \"description\": \"Science is a systematic and logical approach to discovering how the world works.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Entertainment\",\n      \"type\": \"Field\",\n      \"description\": \"Entertainment includes activities designed to provide amusement or enjoyment.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"International Communication\",\n      \"type\": \"Field\",\n      \"description\": \"International communication involves the exchange of information and ideas between people from different countries and cultures.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Business\",\n      \"type\": \"Field\",\n      \"description\": \"Business involves the activities of buying and selling goods and services.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Diplomacy\",\n      \"type\": \"Field\",\n      \"description\": \"Diplomacy is the art and practice of conducting negotiations between representatives of states.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Modern English\",\n      \"type\": \"Language\",\n      \"description\": \"Modern English is the form of English used from the mid-17th century to the present. It is characterized by a more standardized grammar and vocabulary, and it continues to evolve with the influence of technology and globalization.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Great Vowel Shift\",\n      \"type\": \"Linguistic Phenomenon\",\n      \"description\": \"The Great Vowel Shift was a major change in the pronunciation of the English language that took place between the 14th and 18th centuries.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Norman Conquest\",\n      \"type\": \"Historical Event\",\n      \"description\": \"The Norman Conquest of England in 1066 brought significant changes to the English language, leading to the mixing of Old English and Old Norman, which gave rise to Middle English.\",\n      \"attributes\": {}\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Anglo-Saxons\",\n      \"type\": \"Ethnic Group\",\n      \"description\": \"The Anglo-Saxons were a group of Germanic peoples who inhabited and ruled parts of the British Isles from the 5th century until the Norman Conquest in the 11th century.\",\n  