 \"English has solidified its status as a global language, becoming the lingua franca of diplomacy.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"English\",\n      \"Evolved Into\",\n      \"Modern English\",\n      \"English evolved into Modern English, which is the form of the language used today.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"English\",\n      \"Transformed During\",\n      \"Great Vowel Shift\",\n      \"During the Early Modern English period, English underwent the Great Vowel Shift, which altered the pronunciation of many words.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"English language\",\n      \"Developed From\",\n      \"Old English\",\n      \"The English language developed from Old English, which was spoken from the 5th to the 11th century.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"English language\",\n      \"Influenced By\",\n      \"Norman Conquest\",\n      \"The Norman Conquest in the late 11th century significantly influenced the development of the English language, leading to the creation of Middle English.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"English language\",\n      \"Standardized By\",\n      \"William Caxton\",\n      \"William Caxton\\\"s invention of the printing press in the late 15th century helped standardize and spread the use of English across England.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"English language\",\n      \"Exemplified By\",\n      \"William Shakespeare\",\n      \"The works of William Shakespeare exemplify Early Modern English, a period of the English language from the 15th to the 17th century.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"English language\",\n      \"Transformed By\",\n      \"Great Vowel Shift\",\n      \"The Great Vowel Shift, which occurred between the 14th and 18th centuries, transformed the pronunciation of many English words, contributing to the language\\\"s evolution.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"5th century\",\n      \"Period of\",\n      \"Old English\",\n      \"The 5th century is the period when Old English began to be spoken in England.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"5th century\",\n      \"Arrival of\",\n      \"Anglo-Saxons\",\n      \"The 5th century marks the arrival of the Anglo-Saxons in Britain, which led to the development of Old English.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Geoffrey Chaucer\",\n      \"Wrote\",\n      \"The Canterbury Tales\",\n      \"Chaucer wrote \\\"The Canterbury Tales,\\\" which is a significant work in Middle English literature.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Geoffrey Chaucer\",\n      \"Contributed To\",\n      \"Middle English Literature\",\n      \"Chaucer\\\"s works, including \\\"The Canterbury Tales,\\\" are prime examples of Middle English literature, contributing significantly to its development and recognition.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"William Shakespeare\",\n      \"Wrote In\",\n      \"Early Modern English\",\n      \"Shakespeare\\\"s works are written in Early Modern English, which was the form of the language used during his lifetime.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"William Shakespeare\",\n      \"Influenced By\",\n      \"William Caxton\",\n      \"The standardization of the English language, partly due to William Caxton\\\"s introduction of the printing press, influenced the form of English used by Shakespeare.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"William Shakespeare\",\n      \"Contemporary Of\",\n      \"The Normans\",\n      \"Shakespeare lived and wrote during a period that followed the Norman conquest, which had a significant impact on the English language.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Australian English\",\n      \"Variant Of\",\n      \"English\",\n      \"Australian English is a variant of the English language, reflecting the evolution and adaptation of English in the Australian context.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"Australian English\",\n      \"Influenced By\",\n      \"British Empire\",\n      \"The global influence of the British Empire contributed to the development of Australian English, among other English dialects and variations.\"\n    ],\n    [\n      \"entertainment\",\n      \"Uses\",\n      \"English\",\n      \"Entertainment uses English, contributing to its widespread adoption and importance in the global context.\"\n    ]\n  ]\n}"